cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Co-Spiral Framework (CoSF): A bounded research programme on human–AI cognitive coupling"
message: "If you refer to this research programme, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  CoSF is a provisional, bounded research-and-design programme investigating when a
  human–AI working relationship becomes a coupled adaptive system, what cognitive-state
  transitions this produces in the human, and whether pattern-triggered interventions can
  preserve human epistemic agency. It is not a completed theory of cognition and makes no
  claim to be a universal framework.
authors:
  # Name form is settled -- use it identically everywhere from now on.
  #   Family: Pham | Middle: Quang | First: Vien
  #   CFF has no middle-name field, so the middle name lives in given-names.
  #   Renders as "Vien Quang Pham" / cites as "Pham, V. Q."
  # Use this same string on ORCID, Google Scholar, and every submission. Inconsistent
  # author strings are the usual reason one researcher ends up with two citation profiles.
  - family-names: "Pham"
